==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/t͡sɪmt/}}

===Etymology 1===
From late {{inh|de|gmh|zimet}}, from earlier {{m|gmh|zinemīn}}, {{m|gmh|zinment}}, from {{der|de|la|cinnamon}}, {{m|la|cinnamomum}}, from {{der|de|grc|κίνναμον}}, {{m|grc|κινναμωμον}}, from {{der|de|phn}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|g2=n|Zimts|gen2=Zimtes|Zimte}}

# {{lb|de|uncountable}} [[cinnamon]]
#* '''2013''', Hanna Dinkelbach, [https://www.waz.de/staedte/muelheim/zimt-missbrauch-das-risiko-als-letzte-wuerze-id7882312.html Zimt-Missbrauch: Das Risiko als letzte Würze], in: Website of {{w|Westdeutsche Allgemeine Zeitung}}
#*: ''Die Einnahme von '''Zimt''' löst einen schweren Würgereflex aus, weil das Gewürz in Mund und Rachen brennt, erklärt Hower: „Beim Luftholen kann das '''Zimt''' in die Lunge gelangen“.''
#*:: The consumption of '''cinnamon''' provokes a strong pharyngeal reflex because the spice stings in the mouth and throat, Hower explains: “When taking a breath, you can get the '''cinnamon''' into your lungs.”
# {{lb|de|countable}} a particular kind of cinnamon
# {{lb|de|uncountable}} the brownish colour of cinnamon

=====Usage notes=====
* Traditionally and predominantly masculine, but also used as a neuter by some speakers. As a colour it is usually neuter.

